  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 3.1, 'Adaptation of CRDM approach for defining health system challenges' and requirements. Three columns. BUSINESS PROCESS ANALYSIS, 'Think — how do we do our work now?': define goals and objectives, determine the health programme processes to target, map the user journey and workflow, and identify pain points. BUSINESS PROCESS REDESIGN, 'Rethink — how should we do our work now?': examine tasks and workflow, identify inefficiencies, restructure them, and select digital health interventions for the prioritized health system challenges. REQUIREMENTS DEFINITION, 'Describe — how can an information system support our work?': define the tasks for the optimized processes, describe how business rules are implemented, check that the enabling environment can support the interventions, define what the interventions should do from end-user needs, and determine whether existing ICT systems can be leveraged.",
